Decline export indices from 2^18 on in --cfg fuzzing builds

handle_name/handle_level/handle_expr push placeholder slots until the
table reaches the record's "in"/"il"/"ie" index. Skipped and
out-of-order indices are valid (arena other/sparse-name-index) and
kiota's own trimmed fixtures keep original indices up to 145684, so
upstream has no bound: one record with "ie":34888884009 (truncated to
u32) makes a 16 KB export take 24 GB and 53 s natively, and runs a wasm
exec out of fuel or memory. Fuzzing builds decline indices >= 2^18,
which keeps each table at a few MB. Repro in suite-repros.
Upstream: none (no related issue or PR; open issues #3 and #5 are
soundness reports, checked 2026-11-22).

